---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import ProjectList from "../components/ProjectList.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site";
---

<Base title="Work" description="Open source tools for engineer-driven AI, and consulting on AI in platform engineering.">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h1>Work</h1>

		<section aria-labelledby="oss">
			<h2 id="oss">Open source</h2>
			<p class="lede">
				Open source and published under <a href={SITE.github}>github.com/one24-ai</a> as each project is ready.
			</p>
			<h3>pi packages</h3>
			<p class="lede">Extensions for <a href="https://pi.dev">pi</a>, the terminal coding agent I work in every day.</p>
			<ProjectList kind="pi-package" />
			<h3>Other projects</h3>
			<ProjectList kind="project" />
		</section>

		<section aria-labelledby="consulting" class="consulting">
			<h2 id="consulting">Consulting</h2>
			<div class="consulting-body">
				<p>
					I help engineering teams build a culture of efficiency with AI. It’s a smaller shift than most teams
					expect: agents can be fitted to the tools and workflows you already have, so nobody has to change how
					they work. Context switching gets close to free, and output goes up without burning people out.
				</p>
				<p>
					Doing that safely is the hard part, and it’s what I’m good at: agents that work inside your platform’s
					rules, with engineers reviewing and steering, not rubber-stamping. The work tends to look like this:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Mapping AI to your engineers’ existing workflow, with guardrails and habits people keep using.</li>
					<li>Paying down tech debt fast, without building or migrating to new tools and systems.</li>
					<li>Building internal tools and extensions so agents can reach your platform safely.</li>
					<li>Rethinking platform engineering for a world where agents are users of your platform too.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					I take on a small number of engagements, usually through referrals, so I can’t say yes to everything.
					If it sounds like a fit, <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}?subject=Consulting`}>email me</a> with a few
					lines about your team and where you are today.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	h1 {
		font-size: var(--step-4);
		margin-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: var(--step-3);
		margin: 3rem 0 0.75rem;
	}
	.lede {
		color: var(--muted);
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
	}
	h3 {
		font-size: var(--step-1);
		margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
	}
	.consulting {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}
	.consulting-body {
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}
	.consulting-body > * {
		margin: 1em 0 0;
	}
	.consulting-body > :first-child {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.consulting-body li + li {
		margin-top: 0.4em;
	}
</style>
